# Impeccable tool state and the docs it generates.
#
# `.impeccable/` is machine state, not source: hook caches, live-session locks
# and accept-receipts. `DESIGN.md` and `PRODUCT.md` are its generated summaries,
# and they drift from the code the moment the code moves — at the time this rule
# was added DESIGN.md still specified an indigo `brand: '#4F46E5'`, which the
# achromatic repaint had already deleted (`--brand` is byte-identical to
# `--text`), and PRODUCT.md still listed the license and the production domain as
# undecided after both had shipped.
#
# That drift is why they are ignored rather than committed: CLAUDE.md tells
# contributors to CHECK THE DESIGN DOCS before "fixing" something that looks
# off, so a stale one in the repo would send someone to reintroduce exactly what
# a milestone removed. The authoritative documents are `docs/` and
# `src/styles/tokens.css`, which the test suite holds to the code.
.impeccable/
DESIGN.md
PRODUCT.md
